# Guards (route protection)

## Functional guards

- **Use functional guards** - use functional guards (`CanMatchFn`, `CanActivateFn`) instead of classes
- **inject()** - use `inject()` to get dependencies in guards
- **Typing** - guards must be typed (`CanMatchFn`, `CanActivateFn`)

Example:
```typescript
import { inject } from '@angular/core';
import { CanMatchFn, Router } from '@angular/router';

export const langValidateGuard: CanMatchFn = (route, segments) => {
  const router = inject(Router);
  const languageStore = inject(LanguageStore);

  // Validation logic
  const lang = segments[0]?.path?.toUpperCase();
  const isSupportedLang = lang && Languages.includes(lang);

  if (isSupportedLang) {
    languageStore.setCurrentLanguageCode(lang);
    return true;
  }

  // Redirect on invalid language
  const currentLang = languageStore.currentLanguageCode.toLowerCase();
  return router.createUrlTree(['/', currentLang, ...segments.map(s => s.path)]);
};
```

## Guard types

- **CanMatchFn** - check before loading module/component (lazy loading)
- **CanActivateFn** - check before route activation
- **CanDeactivateFn** - check before route deactivation (e.g. leaving a page with unsaved data)
- **CanLoad** - deprecated; use `CanMatchFn` instead

## Applying guards

- **canMatch** - use `canMatch` to check before loading module/component
- **canActivate** - use `canActivate` to check before route activation
- **canDeactivate** - use `canDeactivate` to check before route deactivation
- **Guard array** - multiple guards can be applied: `canMatch: [guard1, guard2]`

Example:
```typescript
{
  path: ':lang',
  canMatch: [langValidateGuard],
  children: [
    {
      path: 'vacancies',
      canActivate: [authGuard],
      loadComponent: () => import('./pages/vacancies/vacancies.component')
        .then(m => m.VacanciesComponent),
    },
  ],
}
```

## Return values

- **true** - allow access to the route
- **false** - deny access (route will not be activated)
- **UrlTree** - redirect to the specified URL

Redirect example:
```typescript
export const authGuard: CanActivateFn = () => {
  const authService = inject(AuthService);

  if (authService.isAuthenticated()) {
    return true;
  }

  // Redirect to login page
  const router = inject(Router);
  return router.createUrlTree(['/login']);
};
```

## Guard logic

- **Minimal logic** - guards should contain only access-check logic
- **Business logic in services** - all business logic belongs in services; guards only call service methods
- **Do not load data** - guards must not load data; only check access conditions

Example:
```typescript
// ❌ Bad - loading data in guard
export const dataGuard: CanActivateFn = () => {
  const dataService = inject(DataService);
  return dataService.loadData().pipe(
    map(data => data !== null)
  );
};

// ✅ Good - access check only
export const authGuard: CanActivateFn = () => {
  const authService = inject(AuthService);
  return authService.isAuthenticated();
};
```

## Async guards

- **Observable/Promise** - guards may return `Observable<boolean | UrlTree>` or `Promise<boolean | UrlTree>`
- **Use RxJS operators** - use operators to handle async operations

Example:
```typescript
export const asyncGuard: CanActivateFn = () => {
  const authService = inject(AuthService);

  return authService.checkAuth$().pipe(
    map(isAuth => isAuth || inject(Router).createUrlTree(['/login']))
  );
};
```
